  "text": "The cc-track hook system now properly outputs single JSON responses. Key insight: the command pattern used here separates execution (runHookCommand) from output handling (applyCommandResult). All commands should follow this pattern - return CommandResult objects and let the framework handle output. The tests added specifically verify no direct stdout writes occur, which is a good pattern for testing command-line tools. Also learned that when Claude Code shows \"Unexpected non-whitespace character after JSON\", it often means duplicate output rather than malformed JSON.",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes"
  ],
